userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: In ΔG = ΔH − TΔS, the enthalpy change sets the y-intercept (spontaneity as T→0) and the entropy change sets the slope, so only when ΔH and ΔS share a sign does raising the temperature flip a process between spontaneous and nonspontaneous at the point where ΔG = 0.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): ΔH sets the intercept and ΔS sets the slope of ΔG versus T, so a process reverses spontaneity with temperature only when ΔH and ΔS have the same sign — and the reversal happens exactly where the line crosses ΔG = 0.
DEMO STEPS: 4 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

